WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.712
This comparison focuses on the preparation problem.

00:00:02.712 --> 00:00:07.962
Structured data is already tabular, so we can usually begin with profiling and cleaning.

00:00:07.962 --> 00:00:11.662
Semi-structured data may need normalization or flattening.

00:00:11.662 --> 00:00:19.522
Unstructured data usually requires feature extraction or annotation before it can be analyzed using ordinary

00:00:19.522 --> 00:00:23.232
tabular methods. Real informatics projects often combine all three forms,

00:00:23.232 --> 00:00:27.532
so understanding the organization tells you what preparation work comes first.

00:00:27.532 --> 00:00:33.787
Connect this idea to a hospital combining patient tables, device JSON, and clinical notes.

00:00:33.787 --> 00:00:38.887
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:38.887 --> 00:00:45.757
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:45.757 --> 00:00:50.782
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:50.782 --> 00:00:56.000
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
